            <ArticleTitle>Regional variation in the diagnosis of asthma among preschool-age children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>189-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To study potential regional variation in asthma diagnostics, we retrospectively analyzed the management of 800 acutely wheezing preschool-age children in two university clinics in Finland. Multivariate modelling indicated that the place of treatment was a strong independent predictor of asthma diagnosis during acute symptoms. Similar regional preferences in diagnostic activity may exist in other countries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
